msgid "The node is already mapped to a device."
msgstr "An riga an taswira node ɗin zuwa wata na'ura."

#: lib/DeviceProvisioner.php
msgid "The node's fabric is not swept by the main poller, so its device could not be polled."
msgstr "Main poller ba ya share fabric ɗin node, don haka ba a iya bincikar na'urarsa ba."

#: lib/DeviceProvisioner.php
msgid "The device does not exist."
msgstr "Na'urar ba ta wanzu ba."

#: lib/DeviceProvisioner.php
msgid "The device is polled by another poller than the one that sweeps this fabric, so it could not read the fabric cache."
msgstr "Wani poller daban ne yake bincikar na'urar ba wanda yake share wannan fabric ba, don haka ba ta iya karanta ajiyar wucin-gadi ta fabric ba."

#: lib/DeviceProvisioner.php
#, php-format
msgid "A device \"%s\" from the %s device template, host name %s, polled by poller %d, with availability checks and SNMP off."
msgstr "Na'ura \"%s\" daga samfurin na'ura na %s, sunan uwar garke %s, wadda poller %d ke bincika, tare da kashe duba samuwa da SNMP."

#: lib/DeviceProvisioner.php
#, php-format
msgid "The %s data query on it, listing the node's ports. It creates no graph and no data source by itself."
msgstr "Tambayar bayanai ta %s a kanta, tana jera tashoshin node. Ba ta ƙirƙirar wani zayyana ko tushen bayanai da kanta ba."

#: lib/DeviceProvisioner.php
#, php-format
msgid "Created by the Fabric plugin for node %s. Its values come from the plugin cache; the host name is a reserved name that is never contacted."
msgstr "Ƙarin Fabric ne ya ƙirƙira don node %s. Ƙimominta suna fitowa daga ajiyar wucin-gadi ta ƙari; sunan uwar garke keɓaɓɓen suna ne da ba a taɓa tuntuɓarsa ba."

#: lib/FabricInput.php
msgid "Name: use 1 to 64 letters, digits, spaces, dots, dashes, or underscores, starting with a letter or digit."
msgstr "Suna: yi amfani da haruffa, lambobi, sarari, ɗigo, layin tsakiya, ko layin ƙasa daga 1 zuwa 64, yana farawa da harafi ko lamba."

#: lib/FabricInput.php
msgid "Backend: choose one of the listed backends."
msgstr "Backend: zaɓi ɗaya daga cikin backends da aka jera."

